kill every Targaryen  everyone who isn't us  is an enemy  so Ilyn bring me his head we take what  is ours  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another Game of Thrones in A  Song of Ice and Fire video today I want  to talk about the five characters George  RR Martin's said would survive his story  all the way back in 1993 George wrote a  3-page letter that outlined his original  plans for a Song of Ice and Fire  he wrote this out just a few years  before his first book a game of Thrones  was published back then his plans for  the story were very different than what  it ended up becoming for those of you  who have not read his original outline I  will put the link down below that way  you can take a look at it for yourself  even though most of it did change it's  still very interesting to get a glimpse  into the story they could have been a  Song of Ice and Fire he still kept some  of the main themes and all of the  characters that he mentioned but most of  them died under very different  circumstances then he originally planned  just as an example he intended on having  Rob die in battle and Joffrey get maimed  on the battlefield but as we all know  Rob died during the red wedding he also  intended on having Catelyn get killed by  the others beyond the wall but we know  she ended up dying at the red wedding  with Rob like I said he still included  all of the characters from his outline  but he did change the direction of their  individual stories one of the most  interesting things from these three  pages is who George said would survive  the entire story back nanny said five  central characters will make it through  all three volumes he only planned on  running a trilogy but even that changed  he goes on to say in a sense my trilogy  is a generational saga telling the life  stories of these five characters three  men and two women the five key players  are tearing in Lannister Daenerys  Targaryen in three of the children of  Winterfell Arya Stark bran stark and the  bastard Jon Snow at the time these were  the only characters George was willing  to say would survive all of the events  to come this revelation caused a debate  between fans because some say these  characters are no longer safe because  George has already changed so much of  this outline but other people say George  would never change the outcome of his  key players  I have even went back and forth on  deciding whether these characters would  live or not both arguments may  some good points but I recently came  across something that may give some more  insight about whether we should believe  any of this outline or not there is a  website called so spake Martin and it's  basically an archive of everywhere  spawns George has ever given regarding A  Song of Ice and Fire as I was on there  reading someone's urges responses to  questions I came across his response to  this outline being leaked on Twitter and  George had some very interesting things  to say about the validity of these three  pages he does admit that this is his  outline but he pretty much says we  should not believe any of it I will post  a link to this conversation down below  as well that way you can read it for  yourself if you would like but I want to  read what he said because this could be  a clue about the fate of these five  characters I believe this conversation  happened while they were attending some  kind of donation dinner possibly for  charity but I'm not exactly sure  it just says donation dinner but this is  what was said I begin writing these  books in 1991 and then I got a TV play  so I put the books aside to really work  on doorways which was a TV pilot and I  did a TV show in 92 to 93 in 1994 I  returned to the books and worked on it  you know up until then in my career as a  writer  I'd always written the entire book  before I hopped it for sale that is  unusual because most writers do chapters  in an outline they write a few chapters  they outline the rest of the book then  they give that to the publisher and the  publisher says okay I'll take that as  some of you may have noticed those who  have been paying very very careful  attention I'm not good with deadlines  and I'm not good with outlines either I  always hated outlines so with fever  dream and with Armageddon rag and with  dying of the light and all about  I wrote the entire book before I turned  it in I did not do chapters and outlines  I sat down I wrote a whole book and I  sent it to my agent and said look here's  the whole book and it's finished that  way I don't have a deadline it would be  finished before it even went on the  market and that worked well for me my  initial thought was to do this the same  way but what happened was in 1994 when I  returned to the books I was very  enthused about it and I said to myself I  really want  right these Game of Thrones books but I  was still in Hollywood and I just lost  all this ground work on doorways the TV  pilot but the studios and network still  wanted to work with me  so I was getting other offers like we  want you to write this movie we want you  to do another TV pilot and you know I  took a couple of them and was still  thinking oh god I'm going to have to put  the book away again cuz I had no  deadline for the book  a game of Thrones so I said to myself  look if I want to get back to being a  novelist I'm gonna have to sell this  even though it's not finished so I had  my 200 pages of Game of Thrones at that  point but they wanted an outline I told  them I don't do outlines I don't know  what's gonna happen I figure it out as I  go along  and that's how I always did it but they  said no we have to have an outline so I  wrote two pages a two-page thing about  what I thought would happen it'll be a  trilogy it'll be three books Game of  Thrones The Dance with Dragons and the  winds of winter  those were the three window titles and  uh it'll be three books and this will  happen and this will happen and this  will happen  I was literally making [ __ ] up and I had  a thought that those two pages were long  forgotten because of course the books  did sell they sold in the United States  and in Great Britain both they sold for  enough money that I didn't have to take  any more Hollywood games so I said no I  don't want any more movies or TV shows  I'm gonna write these books now so I  started writing the books and in the  process I pretty much disregarded the  outline the characters took me off in  entirely different directions so for 20  years I had forgotten that the to page  thing even existed but then someone at  HarperCollins got a new office building  and new conference rooms big conference  rooms that were decorated with books and  stuff like that they ended up naming the  conference rooms after the writers and  in one of the conference rooms they put  up these plastic display cases including  the outline they didn't even ask my  permission they just put it up you know  I was pretty pissed that the outline got  out there that should not have happened  outlines and letters like that are meant  only for the eyes of the editor they  should not go on public display  you  all right so as you can see George is  basically saying that outline was made  only for the purposes of getting the  ball rolling on completing the books if  what he said here was true then that  means he pretty much just made things up  so he could turn in an outline and get  the project sold he literally says I was  making up [ __ ] I said this will happen  and this will happen and this will  happen which basically means he was just  saying yada yada yada now of course you  could say George has to say things like  this that way he can cast some doubt  over the outline that way people won't  know any of his intentions of how the  story will end when you consider how  much has already changed from the  outline I don't think it's out of the  realm of possibility that he could kill  off some of those five key characters  for good some could even argue that  George has already foreshadowed some of  the characters deaths depending on how  you interpret the text from the books I  do however find it odd that George was  so pissed  this was leaked if he was just making  [ __ ] up like he says then why should he  worry about it being made public  he already changed most of it so what is  the problem if you was really just  making [ __ ] up by saying this will  happen and that will happen and this  will happen then you shouldn't have to  worry about something getting spoiled  I do believe most of these five  characters will live throughout each  book but I would not bet that all of  them will regardless of what George has  to say about the outline Jon Snow could  easily die in battle as well as Arya  Stark now some people think just because  Arya is George's wife's favorite  character that means she is destined to  live but I would not be so sure about  that there are also theories about bran  stark dying once magic comes to an end  and there are theories about bran being  than I came which would mean Jon would  most likely have to kill him there are  just so many different possibilities I  have made a video about this outlined  before so I don't want to repeat  anything from the other video but I  wanted to show you what George had to  say about it because I had never seen  his response before until I came across  it last night let me know what you think  about some of the things he said do you  really believe he was just making things  up in order to turn in an outline  or do you think he's just trying to  mislead us into believing it's all wrong  I don't want to call George a liar but  since he was still mad about it being  posted that makes me question what he  had to say about it are all five of  these characters still going to live or  is george trying to make us think they  are in just as much danger as some of  the minor characters put all your  thoughts on this down below 